**Goal** — Make worktrees of one repository one project, by sharing one `isSameProject(remoteA, remoteB)` predicate (with normalization) between `claimProjectIdentity` and `checkInitCollision`.

**Motivation** — `.nax/config.json` is tracked, so every worktree carries the same `name` and derives the same `projectKey`. `claimProjectIdentity` throws `RUN_NAME_COLLISION` on any workdir mismatch, while `checkInitCollision` already accepts the same case by raw remote equality. They disagree about what "the same project" means, and `nax migrate --merge` is the only workaround. This story must land AFTER US-002 because relaxing the identity guard without the locking changes would let two processes mutate the shared `~/.nax/<projectKey>/` tree.

**Approach** — One `isSameProject` predicate with remote normalization, shared by `claimProjectIdentity` and `checkInitCollision`. Depends on US-002: this is the story that legalizes concurrency, and it must not land before the locks that make it safe.

**Scope** — In: `src/runtime/same-project.ts` with `isSameProject(remoteA: string | null, remoteB: string | null): boolean` and the normalization rules. `claimProjectIdentity` accepts a workdir-mismatched record when `isSameProject` holds, refreshing `lastSeen` and leaving stored `workdir` at the registered value. `checkInitCollision` replaces `sameRemote` with `isSameProject` and retains the `sameWorkdir` (both remotes null + workdirs equal) branch. Out: tooling visibility (US-003), status-file workdir (US-005), curator fix (US-006).

**Interface**
```typescript
// src/runtime/same-project.ts
export function isSameProject(remoteA: string | null, remoteB: string | null): boolean;
// Returns false when either argument is null.
// Normalization, applied to each side before comparison:
//   1. lowercase
//   2. strip scheme (e.g. https://, git://, ssh://)
//   3. strip credentials (user:pass@, user@)
//   4. strip any port (:1234 after host)
//   5. convert scp-style "host:path" to "host/path"
//   6. strip one trailing ".git"
//   7. strip trailing slash
// Comparison is over the resulting "host/path" — host is significant; forks on different hosts remain different projects.

// src/runtime/paths.ts
export async function claimProjectIdentity(
  projectKey: string,
  workdir: string,
  remoteUrl: string | null,
): Promise<void>;
// Behavior change: when `existing.workdir !== workdir` and `isSameProject(remoteUrl, existing.remoteUrl)` holds,
// refresh `lastSeen` and leave the stored `workdir` at the registered value.
// Otherwise (different remotes OR both remotes null with different workdirs) the existing
// RUN_NAME_COLLISION throw is unchanged.

// src/cli/init.ts
export async function checkInitCollision(
  name: string,
  currentWorkdir: string,
  currentRemote: string | null,
): Promise<InitCollisionResult>;
// Replaces `sameRemote` (raw string equality) with `isSameProject(currentRemote, identity.remoteUrl)`.
// Keeps `sameWorkdir` branch unchanged (both remotes falsy + workdirs equal → no collision).

// Barrel re-export: src/runtime/index.ts gains `export { isSameProject } from "./same-project";`
```

**Failure handling** — `git remote get-url origin` failure or non-git project → `remoteUrl` stays null and identity falls back to exact workdir equality (existing behaviour, no change).

**Goal** — Stamp `run.workdir` into the status file through `StatusWriterContext`, and build run IDs in one place with a workdir hash, called once per run including on the resume path.

**Motivation** — Two worktrees of one project can both produce `run-<iso>` IDs at the same ISO timestamp and clobber each other's log file and status.json. A single producer keyed on (workdir hash, timestamp) makes the ID unique per checkout while keeping filename safety (no path separators). Stamping `run.workdir` into the status file gives external readers a way to attribute which checkout wrote the run without parsing log lines.

**Approach** — Stamp `run.workdir` into the status file through `StatusWriterContext`, and build run IDs in one place with a workdir hash, called once per run including on the resume path. No dependencies.

**Scope** — In: `src/execution/run-id.ts` with `buildRunId(workdir, now)`. `StatusWriterContext` and `RunStateSnapshot` gain optional `workdir`; `buildStatusSnapshot` reads it; `NaxStatusFile.run.workdir` is the new optional field. The run-setup sole StatusWriter construction site (lines 173-180, with `workdir` already in scope from `:142`) supplies it. `run()` accepts an optional `runId` and uses `buildRunId` when absent; `nax resume` builds one and passes it so the resumed log file matches the run's ID. Out: identity-by-remote (US-004), tooling visibility (US-003), curator fix (US-006).

**Interface**
```typescript
// src/execution/run-id.ts
export function buildRunId(workdir: string, now: Date): string;
// Workdir component is a short hash of the absolute working directory — any hash will do, but not the basename
// (which collides for `git worktree add ../repo-feat`). Output contains no path separator and no character
// outside [A-Za-z0-9._-] because it is interpolated into filenames and directory names at more than 10 sites.
// Retains millisecond precision from `now`.

// src/execution/status-writer.ts
export interface StatusWriterContext {
  runId: string;
  feature: string;
  startedAt: string;
  dryRun: boolean;
  startTimeMs: number;
  pid: number;
  workdir?: string;   // NEW: optional, propagated to NaxStatusFile.run.workdir
}

// src/execution/status-file.ts
export interface NaxStatusFile {
  version: 1;
  run: {
    id: string;
    feature: string;
    workdir?: string;   // NEW: optional; readers tolerate absence in pre-existing status files
    startedAt: string;
    status: "running" | "completed" | "failed" | "stalled" | "crashed" | "precheck-failed" | "cost-limit" | "aborted";
    dryRun: boolean;
    pid: number;
    crashedAt?: string;
    crashSignal?: string;
  };
  // ... existing fields
}

export interface RunStateSnapshot {
  // ... existing fields
  workdir?: string;   // NEW
}

export function buildStatusSnapshot(state: RunStateSnapshot): NaxStatusFile;
// Reads `state.workdir` and projects it onto `snapshot.run.workdir` when present.

// src/execution/runner.ts (line 176)
export async function run(options: {
  // ... existing fields
  runId?: string;   // NEW
}): Promise<RunResult>;
// When `options.runId` is supplied, uses it directly.
// When absent, generates `buildRunId(workdir, new Date())` once per run.

// src/commands/resume.ts (line 191-201)
// Replace the local second-resolution ID derivation with a buildRunId call,
// passing the result as `runId` to `run()`. Log file path uses the same ID
// (`runs/<feature>/runs/<runId>.jsonl`), so log filename matches the run it records.
```

**Failure handling** — `status.run.workdir` is optional; readers (TUI, `nax status`) tolerate its absence in files written before this change.

**Goal** — Replace the positional fallback in the curator's metrics reader with a fail-closed match on `runId`, and guard the two shapes that must not change.

**Motivation** — `metrics.json` is a project-level append shared by every feature, locked across processes through `withPathFileLock` (`src/metrics/tracker.ts:20`), so two features' entries coexist and under concurrency `runs.find(r => r.runId === context.runId) ?? runs.at(-1)` attributes another feature's stories to this run's observations. The sibling reader `collectFromReviewAudit` (`src/plugins/builtin/curator/collect.ts:209`) already guards this case by feature name and time window at `:220-227` — the class was anticipated, and one reader was missed.

**Approach** — Replace the positional fallback with a fail-closed match, and guard the two shapes that must not change. Depends on US-004.

**Scope** — In: `collectFromMetrics` returns an empty observations array and warns when no entry matches `context.runId`; preserves the matching-entry case; preserves the corrupt-file skip behaviour. The audit-table disposition from the spec is the binding source of which readers to touch: only `collectFromMetrics` is the defect; `collectFromReviewAudit` (`src/plugins/builtin/curator/collect.ts:209`), `getLastRun` (`src/metrics/aggregator.ts:194`), `<project>-<feature>-<runId>` directory (`src/pipeline/subscribers/registry.ts:53`), `status-features.ts:249-287`, and `metrics/tracker.ts:20` (writer) are NOT changed. Out: identity, locking, run-attribution work in other stories.

